WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.703
Idea. Think about a group project. When everyone cares, the work is done quickly and well. When people don't care, mistakes creep in and some drop out.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:20.764
Motivated employees work harder, make fewer mistakes and give better customer service. They are also more likely to stay. Keeping staff is called retaining them.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:34.443
Method. Staff turnover is the rate at which employees leave and have to be replaced. High turnover is costly, because every replacement means advertising, interviewing and training again.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:50.304
Staff who stay build up product knowledge and skills they pass on to customers and colleagues. That is why some businesses pay above the minimum wage: to attract better applicants, reward skilled staff, and stop them moving to competitors.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:01:04.795
To explain, give one reason: higher productivity, better service, lower staff turnover, or attracting skilled staff. Explain how motivation leads to it, then carry the chain to costs, sales or profit.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:17.876
Worked example. Here is a real question from Paper one R in June twenty twenty-two. Explain one benefit for a business of motivating its employees. It is worth three marks.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:25.030
Mark one is the benefit. Motivated employees are more likely to stay, so staff turnover is lower.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:33.779
Mark two explains it. The business does not have to keep advertising vacancies, interviewing applicants and training replacements.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:48.813
Mark three is the consequence. It saves time and money that can be used elsewhere, and experienced staff give better service, helping sales. This explanation is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:59.185
Common mistake. A common mistake is explaining how to motivate, such as paying a bonus, when the question asks why motivation matters.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:06.777
Another mistake is writing that staff work harder, then stopping. Carry the chain on to an effect on the business.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:21.017
Your turn. Now you try. A hair salon loses three stylists every year to rival salons. Explain one benefit to the salon of keeping its stylists motivated. Pause and decide.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:38.123
Answer. Motivated stylists are more likely to stay, so staff turnover falls. The salon recruits and trains fewer new stylists, and regular customers keep the stylist they trust. So hiring costs fall, and customers keep coming back.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:48.957
Remember the chain: give one reason, explain how motivation causes it, then finish with costs, sales or profit. Now try the practice questions.
